{
  "dom_id": "step-e5334",
  "name": "Example: Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point",
  "problem": "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(4,4).$",
  "worked_solution": "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\ny^2  = 4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(4,4),$ we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(4) \\\\ 16 & =16p \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(1)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
